BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sea Chantey Sing
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T160000
UID:260515cD1lCrCnak-5ly2Ol0rj6w
DESCRIPTION:We’ll have two Chantey Sings simultaneously: an a cappella s
 ing in the hold of the C. A. Thayer\, and a parallel session in one of the
  Coal Sheds. The Coal Shed event meets ADA requirements. Both events are f
 ree and open to the public\; however\, the hold of the Thayer is limited t
 o 49 people by the Fire Marshall and is not ADA accessible. We will take b
 reaks and rotate participants from the Coal Shed.\n\nDue to limited space 
 on the C. A. Thayer\, RESERVATIONS ARE REQUIRED by email to casey\\_fenton
 @nps.gov.\n\nThe Coal Sheds are large rooms formerly used by the Navy to s
 tore coal. One of them is now occupied by the Mare Island Brewing Company\
 , and food and beverages can be purchased there. One of them has retail sp
 ace and facilities. Most of them are empty and open on the side facing the
  water\, and we use one of the those for the Chantey Sing.\n\nThe organize
 rs would love to have more instrumental participation at the Coal Shed sin
 g. Amateurs are especially encouraged\, as well as seasoned chantey player
 s--we'd like this event to be a welcoming and low-pressure place for peopl
 e who are just learning or rediscovering music and chantey folklore.\n\nNe
 w to the Chantey Sing? This is a session of sea chanteys and other types o
 f seafaring\, fishing\, and rowing songs. All are welcome to lead songs\, 
 and admission is free. For more information\, please email casey\\_fenton@
 nps.gov. The sings are part of the interpretive programming at San Francis
 co Maritime National Historical Park.
LOCATION:Mare Island Promenade
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/1410225357538231
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
