BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:19 Voices in Solidarity at The Lost Church
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T190000
UID:260502qFgppARuIkCkxj_yn7yCHw
DESCRIPTION:Bay Area musicians/songwriters are once again meeting the mome
 nt with their voices to help raise funds for peace and justice. In light o
 f the recent challenges to democracy as we know it\, Bay Area songwriter D
 eborah Crooks has organized another fundraiser featuring  women-lend musi
 cal acts to take place at The Lost Church-Santa Rosa on **Saturday\, May 1
 6\, 2026\, 4-7pm**. This will be the fifth 19 Voices in Solidarity event\,
  the number 19 referencing the 19th Amendment which famously gave women th
 e right to vote in 1920. All proceeds from the show will go to the America
 n Civil Liberties Union and the Peace and Justice Center of Sonoma County\
 , organizations dedicated to defending and protecting our fundamental free
 doms.\n\nThe show will feature performances by Sonoma County and Greater B
 ay Area-based artists including Audio Angel\, Brightdarkdawn\, Deborah Cro
 oks\, Marina Crouse\, Roberta Donnay\, Aireene Espiritu\, Shockheaded Elle
 n\, Maggie Forti\, Anna Jae\, Ellie James\, Cecilia Long\, Lindsey McFarla
 nd\, Megan McLaughlin\, Amy Obenski\, Sara Rodenburg\, Zoe Sameth\, Stepha
 nie Siehr\, Callie Watts  Mindi Levine\, aka ‘Mindi in the Morning\,’
  from The KRUSH FM\, will serve as emcee.
LOCATION:The Lost Church
URL:https://tinyurl.com/19VoicesinSolidaritySR 
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Live Music Saturday
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T200000
UID:260502LQdG9jmubUK5BlxRpKgH6Q
DESCRIPTION:Joyce Grant Vallejo local singer\, Joyce Grant returns to the 
 Ferry Taproom with her powerful mix of jazz\, blues\, and R&B. Joyce Grant
  singer/songwriter\, determined at an early age that she was going to be a
  singer and spent her elementary and high school days performing in choir 
 and musical theater. She is the great-great-niece of famed ragtime compose
 r Scott Joplin and has written lyrics to four of his songs. She has partic
 ipated in the West Coast Ragtime Festival for several years. City Swing st
 arted a new chapter in 2007 with jazz singer Joyce Grant. She is the lead 
 vocalist for City Swing\, an 18 piece big band. Grant has been singing jaz
 z in Bay Area venues for over 20 years. A mezzo-soprano with a voice like 
 dark honey\, Grant has a performance resume which includes a wide range of
  venues including the Empire Plush Room and Zingari Ristaurante in San Fra
 ncisco\, the Ledson Hotel in Sonoma\, Sam's Chowder House & Cetrella in Ha
 lf Moon Bay\, the Sticky Rice in Fairfield\, Carneros in Napa\, Slates in 
 Walnut Creek\, Joe's of Lafayette\, and the Woodminster Amphitheater just 
 to name a few. Born in Texarkana\, the town where Scott Joplin was raised\
 , Grant moved to Oakland as a child where she started singing with the Nor
 th Oakland Baptist Church Youth Choir. Since that time she has earned the 
 respect of singers and musicians alike performing professionally in San Fr
 ancisco\, the East Bay\, Walnut Creek\, Napa Valley and beyond. Her unique
  shows consist of a blend of jazz\, blues\, country western\, Rhythm and B
 lues\, and funk. Her vocal interpretations range from sensitive to powerfu
 l to cheeky over a broad spectrum of charts. Joyce Grant is a member of AS
 CAP.
LOCATION:Ferry Taproom
URL:https://www.mareislandbrewingco.com/events/live-music-saturday-0516202
 6
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:INTO THE LIGHT: Light-filled aintings by Katy Boggs
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T170000
UID:2605014VbGAyKSo06rxqN77xRhPw
DESCRIPTION:Katy's paintings are an exploration of light—how it shapes f
 orm\, reveals color\, and defines what we see.\n\n"I am drawn to moments w
 here light is felt as much as seen: filtering through dense leaves\, tower
 ing in the crowns of trees\, glinting off cresting waves\, or softening in
 to the quiet glow of a sunset. Light is everywhere\; without it\, there is
  no seeing. Beyond its physical presence\, it also carries a deeper resona
 nce as a symbol of hope. In a time of uncertainty\, this work seeks to bri
 ng light into the image\, both visually and metaphorically."\n\nReception:
  April 25\, 4 to 6 pm.
LOCATION:Sebastopol Gallery
URL:http://sebastopolgallery.com
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
