BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wilderness First Aid Course
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T083000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T180000
UID:2604129qNyqMeeeEOYO7VyuToJKQ
DESCRIPTION:Lead by Safety Training Pros\, classes are fun with l
 ots of hands-on skills practice. The emphasis is on making good
  decisions by staying calm and safe\, doing a good patient asse
 ssment\, and having good communication and leadership. \n\nJoin ou
 r classes\, where it is safe to learn and OK to make mistakes.
  Wilderness First Aid is 16 hours (two 8-hour days) and focuses
  on practicing skills and covering patient assessment\, shock and
  bleeding\, head and spinal injuries\, wounds\, musculoskeletal in
 juries\, and heat and cold illnesses. It also includes a half-da
 y of outdoor scenario practice of first aid and leadership skill
 s. \n\nGain the tools and knowledge to handle a wilderness first
  aid emergency. Registration includes day use fee and class mate
 rials. Successful completion of the class includes a Wilderness F
 irst Aid certificate.\n\nThe instructor will additionally offer a 
 one-hour CPR/AED course immediately after the Wilderness First Aid
  course. The course will focus on both adults and children and
  comes with a 2-year certification.\n\nThe group camp will be av
 ailable for those who wish to camp on Saturday and Sunday night
  at no additional cost. Please reach out to alma@sonomaecologycen
 ter.org if you plan on taking advantage of this opportunity.
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/wfamay2026
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sonoma Repair Fair + Clothing Swap
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T130000
UID:2604125iqHYo2Vxk2wGGOSUGgE6w
DESCRIPTION:Do you have a lamp\, small appliance\, textile\, or bike in ne
 ed of repair?\n\nBring it to the Repair Fair!‍ ‍\n\nVolunteers and spe
 cialized repair professionals will be on-hand to repair\\* your items.  
 We ask that you stay with your item while it's being fixed\, so you can le
 arn tips for future maintenance\, how to shop for repairable goods\, and e
 ven how to repair things yourself!  \n\nIf you’d like to bring an it
 em to repair\, please register the item here: https://www.reusealliance.or
 g/rf-reg \\(Pre-registering allows us to prepare for your item!\\)\n\nThis
  is a free public event.\n\nThis event will also include a Clothing Swap. 
 Please bring clothing items and accessories \\(clean and in good shape\\) 
 to share and bring home something new to you!\n\n\\*We cannot guarantee yo
 ur item\\(s\\) will be repaired\, depending on the existing damage or brea
 kage\, ability of volunteer fixers\, and availability of materials for rep
 air. Note: we cannot work on microwaves\, repair screens on cell phones/co
 mputer devices\, or perform any welding/brazing\, but we are happy to ref
 er you to professionals who can. In addition\, the textile department is n
 ot able to perform the following:\n\nReplacing zippers\n\nRepairing shoes\
 , leather\, or vinyl materials\n\nPerforming alterations \\(making garment
 s bigger/smaller\\)\n\nReplacing rivets/grommets\n\nHemming certain fabric
 s \\(stretchy fabric\, sleek/luxury fabrics e.g. prom dresses\\)\n\nIf you
  are in need of garment hemming\, we require that you please pin your garm
 ent to the desired length before you arrive.\n\nJoin Us!\n\nDoes fixing th
 ings sound like a fun way to spend a Saturday afternoon?  Or want to help
  out in other ways?  We need you!\n\nEmail volunteer@reusealliance.org or
  sign up here: https://www.reusealliance.org/rf-volunteer
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://www.reusealliance.org/events/sonoma-repair-fair
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:BLS Certification Class (American Heart Association)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T090000
UID:260408ODgm5W1IYU-IzY2vaimdAQ
DESCRIPTION:BLS Certification Class \\(AHA\\) - In Person\, Instructor-Led
 \n\nAmerican Heart Association BLS certification class \\(in-person\, inst
 ructor-led class in our Rohnert Park classroom\\). BLS \\(Basic Life Suppo
 rt\\) is the required CPR class for healthcare providers. Includes cardiac
  and respiratory arrest management\, CPR\, AED use\, and choking treatment
  for all ages. This class is appropriate for initial BLS or BLS renewal.\n
 \nVive CPR is an American Heart Association \\(AHA\\) Training Site. AHA "
 BLS Provider" certifications are issued on the same day.\n\nWe also offer 
 Blended Learning BLS certification courses \\(online course plus in-person
  Skills Session\\).\n\nLearn from a top-rated\, local CPR training company
  with over 900 5-star reviews! Our classes are fun\, engaging\, and expert
 ly taught by experienced first responders.\n\nLearn More & Enroll: https:/
 /vivecpr.com/class/bls-certification/\n\nQuestions? Call/text \\(707\\) 61
 2-3277 or https://vivecpr.com/contact
LOCATION:Vive CPR
URL:https://vivecpr.com/class/bls-certification
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
