UID:260224F9wcuXQD_E2j5wd9Hq7mkQ
DESCRIPTION:Born in a small country town in New England and into a musical
  family\,\n\nStreet singer- turned songwriter- Reed Foehl’s  music  tell
 s stories of the human condition with a lyric and voice that push the boun
 daries while paying homage to tradition. Dusty and patient his music is ge
 nuine Folk/Americana. He was nominated for a grammy for his song “Fly”
  which was covered by country legend “ Lee Ann Womack”.  His five stud
 io albums have put him on the map of the publishing world\, garnering plac
 ements in both film and television. Foehl released his 6th studio record 
 “Wild Wild Love” recorded in Austin TX with The Band Of Heathens in 20
 23. He is currently working on his 7th studio album in Woodstock NY.
