BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mapping Northern End of the Camino Real
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T120000
UID:260514kINdPeiyg0-SGDePgQDGfw
DESCRIPTION:The path of the Camino Real connecting the 21 missions in Cali
 fornia has long been a topic of interest. The portion of the trail north o
 f San Francisco in Sonoma has been less studied. Much of the trail can be 
 inferred from an assortment of maps while written records add to the evide
 nce. Dr. Meyerhof has found overlooked material that sheds light on the la
 st portion of this trail as it crossed the ridges of the Sonoma Mountains 
 that separate the Petaluma Valley from the Sonoma Valley. Dr. Peter Meyerh
 of is a retired dentist and cell biologist. His passion has been researchi
 ng the early history of California\, particularly Sonoma County. His histo
 rical research has taken him to primary sources in archives and libraries 
 across the country in order to find new material for publications and pres
 entations. Advanced registration required to access the Zoom link.
URL:https://events.sonomalibrary.org/event/mapping-nothern-end-camino-real
 -109094
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
