BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Vallejo Project Open House
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260517T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260517T140000
UID:260514GZISGfxTYkyjmSnZH2jphQ
DESCRIPTION:Vallejo Project invites community members\, educators\, health
 care advocates\, local leaders\, and supporters to attend a special Open H
 ouse on Sunday\, May 17\, from 11:00 AM to 2:00 PM at 2160 Sacramento Stre
 et\, Vallejo\, CA.\n\nThe event will showcase an original communal living 
 housing model designed to bring people together in safe\, dignified\, and 
 healing ways while addressing the root causes of instability through commu
 nity care and wellness-centered living.\n\nThis evolving model focuses on 
 social determinants of health\, including healthy eating\, mindfulness\, e
 xercise\, environmental stewardship\, and connection to nature through gar
 dening and animal care. Visitors will have the opportunity to tour the pro
 perty\, meet residents and youth participants\, and experience firsthand h
 ow community-based living can foster resilience\, belonging\, and hope.\n\
 nVallejo Project’s approach combines housing support with opportunities 
 for personal growth\, vocational development\, urban agriculture\, and wel
 lness practices that encourage healing and long-term stability.\n\n“This
  is about more than housing\,” said Adjoa McDonald\, Founder of Vallejo 
 Project. “It’s about rebuilding community\, restoring dignity\, and cr
 eating environments where people can thrive mentally\, physically\, and sp
 iritually.”\n\nThe Open House will include: • Tours of the communal li
 ving space and garden • Demonstrations of wellness and sustainability pr
 actices • Opportunities to meet youth leaders and community members • 
 Conversations about innovative housing solutions and community healing\n\n
 The event is open to the public\, and all are welcome.
LOCATION:Unity Garden
URL:https://www.vallejoproject.org/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
