BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Beginners Watercolor 4-wk Class: Landscapes
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260517T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260517T150000
UID:260508y8UgoxXgEk28iT_GCYpPig
DESCRIPTION:PLEASE NOTE: The first class is on Sat. May 9th\, 1-3 PM\n\nSt
 arting with foundational drawing skills and then moving into watercolor pa
 inting landscapes\, this class will explore brush strokes\, color\, compos
 ition\, and tone to illustrate striking landscapes that capture the detail
  and atmosphere of the natural world. \n\nWatercolor is one of the most c
 onducive media for depicting nature in its purest form. Learn a step-by-st
 ep process for painting watercolor landscapes as we explore light and text
 ure to capture the gorgeousness of Sonoma County. \n\n-Supplies: watercol
 or notebook\, no smaller than 8 x 11\; paint\; brushes.\n\nSat.\, May 9t
 h and Sunday May 17th\, 24th\, 31st
LOCATION:Full Circle Studio
URL:https://www.taradickinson.com/lets-create/art-classes
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Concert honors Supreme Court Justice Thurgood Marshall
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260517T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260517T180000
UID:260508oxWoqQW6AU-UvB41RovJ3A
DESCRIPTION:Not everyone knows that the Episcopal Church named Thurgood Ma
 rshall\, the first African-American Justice of the U.S. Supreme Court\, a 
 saint. His feast day is celebrated on May 17\, the anniversary of the mile
 stone 1954 U.S. Supreme Court decision Brown v. Board of Education. At tha
 t time Marshall was the chief legal counsel for the  NAACP\; he successfu
 lly argued that segregation in schools was unconstitutional. To honor Mars
 hall\, St. Paul's Episcopal Church presents a Choral Evensong on Sunday\, 
 May 17. Director of Music Paul Blanchard will play a number of beautiful c
 lassical selections\, accompanying the St. Paul's choir. Admission to the 
 5 p.m. concert is free. Donations to the church's outreach ministries will
  be gratefully accepted. Those who cannot attend in person are invited to 
 watch the concert online at www.stpauls-healdsburg.org/sunday\\_organ\\_s
 eries. The church is located at the corner of East and Matheson Streets\, 
 one block east of Healdsburg's downtown Plaza.
LOCATION:St. Paul's Episcopal Church
URL:http://www.stpauls-healdsburg.org
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Angels in America\, Part One: Millennium Approaches
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260517T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260517T170000
UID:260508m9SjPECtmUGQ_ZLxg2F-zw
DESCRIPTION:**By Tony Kushner**\n\n**Directed by Steven David Martin**\n\n
 Set in 1980s New York City\, a gay man is abandoned by his lover when he c
 ontracts the AIDS virus\, while closeted Mormon lawyer’s marriage to his
  pill-popping wife stalls. And that’s just the tip of the iceberg. Widel
 y described as one of the greatest plays of the 20th century\, *Angels i
 n America* is a complex\, dynamic\, sometimes surrealistic examination of
  the AIDS crisis and homosexuality in the United States\, while touching o
 n universal issues including change\, loss\, identity\, and the challenges
  of finding community in an increasingly fractured society.\n\n**Content W
 arning**: Please be advised that this production contains simulated sex\, 
 graphic depictions of illness\, staged violence\, and is intended for matu
 re (17+) audiences only.\n\nApprox. 3 hours with 2 intermissions.\n\n**May
  8th\, 9th\, 10th\, \\*14th\, 15th\, 16th\, 17th\, 22nd\, 23rd\, 24th.**\n
 \n**Friday and Saturday Shows:** 7:30 PM\n\n**Sunday Matinee:** 2:00 PM\
 n\n**\\*Value Thursday:** 7:30 PM (Pay What You Can)\n\nDoors open 30 min
 utes before showtime.
LOCATION:The Raven Performing Arts Theater
URL:https://raventheater.org/events/angels-in-america-part-one-millennium-
 approaches/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:ASL Sourdough Baking
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260517T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260517T160000
UID:260508iQ-QO9Bb2EqwlIdubQUkdw
DESCRIPTION:Schedule\n\nSunday\, May 17\, 2026 1:00 PM – 4:00 PM\n\nLoca
 tion\n\nRoom 109\, Rotary Kitchen\n\nExperience Level\n\nAll Levels\n\nEve
 nt Categories: Bilingual\, Culinary Arts\n\nAge\\(s\\)\n\n18 and older\n\n
 Registration\n\nRegistration Cost:\n\n$75\n\nThis hands-on\, three-hour wo
 rkshop provides you with a simplified\, “no-fail” method for baking pr
 ofessional-quality rustic bread at home.\n\nAbout the Class\n\nDesigned fo
 r busy beginners\, this class focuses on a straightforward approach that i
 s highlighted by a flexible schedule. You will master the essential skills
  needed to maintain a healthy starter\, learn the basics of bulk fermentat
 ion\, and practice techniques to bake a crusty\, flavorful loaf. What you 
 will learn:\n\nStarter Basics: How to feed\, store\, and revive your sourd
 ough starter.\n\nSourdough Bread Basics: How to adjust your recipe\, mix\,
  fold\, and proof your dough.\n\nShaping\, Scoring and Baking Techniques:
   How to shape the dough and use a blade\, then options to bake it to cre
 ate a beautiful loaf.\n\nParticipants will leave with complete instruction
 s\, a jar of active starter\, parchment paper\, a scoring tool\, and bread
  dough ready to bake the following morning. Dough container provided.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/asl-sourdough-baking-2/
