BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fifth Annual Call of the Wild Festival & Free Guided Hike
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260517T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260517T150000
UID:260425EYvu241Rok-yfdY26iImZQ
DESCRIPTION:The Fifth Annual Call of the Wild Festival is a fun-filled com
 munity celebration presented by Jack London Park Partners. It's also part 
 of the yearlong celebration of Jack London's 150th birthday.\n\nA free Fam
 ily and Friends Hike\, \\(normally $10 per person\\) will be offered at 10
  a.m.-1 p.m.  \n\nThe guided hike will pass through the canopy of redwoo
 ds and mixed evergreens on the way to London Lake\, with an option to cont
 inue to the majestic Ancient Redwood\, estimated to be between 1\,800-2\,0
 00 years old.  This is a moderate hike of approximately 3.5 miles round t
 rip with some elevation gain. Participants should wear sturdy shoes\, brin
 g plenty of water\, and snacks\, and dress in layers.  Dogs are not allow
 ed on backcountry trails.\n\nReservations for the Family and Friends Hike 
 are required and can be made at https://jacklondonpark.com/events/family-h
 ike-2026/.\n\nA full day of family-friendly activities\, plus tasty foods 
 and drinks are planned:\n\n11 a.m. and 1 p.m.          Guided tou
 rs to the Wolf House\n\n11 a.m. - 2 p.m.                Jack
  London Treasure Map art project with ArtEscape\n\n11 a.m. - 2 p.m.    
             Face painting with ArtEscape\n\n11 a.m. - 2 p.m. 
                Country musician Tommy Thomsen will perform l
 ive in the Winery ruins\, courtesy of Music in Place. \n\n11 a.m. - 3 p.m
 .                Beauty Ranch Bingo & The Adventure Quest Pa
 ssport\n\nPick up a Beauty Ranch Bingo card or an Adventure Quest Passport
  and let it guide you through Jack London’s inspiring history\, agricult
 ure\, and innovation. Complete a card or passport quest to receive a prize
 .\n\n11 a.m.-3 p.m.                  Blacksmith demonstrat
 ion in front of the Distillery building.\n\n11 a.m.-3 p.m.        
           Tractor-pulled hayrides around the Beauty Ranch.\n\n11 
 a.m.-3 p.m.                  Additional kid-friendly games
  and crafts in the Winery Ruins.\n\n11 a.m.-3 p.m.            
       Tri Tip Trolley will serve savory favorites and comfort food cl
 assics\n\n11 a.m.-3 p.m.                  Kona Ice.  Coo
 l off with a refreshing cup of tropical shaved ice in the spirit of Jack L
 ondon’s adventures in the South Seas.\n\n11 a.m.-3 p.m.         
          Treat yourself to a cider with Tilted Shed Ciderworks.\n\
 n11:30 a.m.-12:30 p.m.    Storytelling in the House of Happy Walls Muse
 um.   Brandon Spars will share stories from “Tales of the Fish Patrol\
 ,” inspired by Jack London’s experiences as a teenager on the San Fran
 cisco Bay in the early 1890s.\n\nSpars is an educator\, author\, and accom
 plished storyteller who weaves together ancient history and narrative\, wi
 th four published books\, a TEDx talk\, and performances at renowned story
 telling festivals\, including the National Storytelling Festival.\n\n1 p.m
 .                                Guided tour
  of Jack London’s Beauty Ranch\n\nThe Call of the Wild Festival is suppo
 rted by the City of Sonoma with funding from the City’s Recreation and C
 ommunity Services Program.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/events/call-of-the-wild-festival-2026/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
