BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Spring Garden Tours: Osmosis Landscape and Meditation Garden
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260519T093000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260519T113000
UID:260506rW3GBrYjj0a4IuPpggN5BQ
DESCRIPTION:We invite you to join us for a walk through our landscape sanc
 tuary with aesthetic pruning\n\nexpert Michael Alliger and Osmosis founder
  Michael Stusser. They will share a detailed look at\n\nthe plantings and 
 pruning styles we have used to create Japanese style gardens over 40 years
 \n\nusing deer proof and drought resistant plantings suitable for our Cali
 fornia climate. The design\n\nintentions for the rock arrangements will be
  shared from the view point of the way in which\n\nthey are placed to tell
  the ancient Zen tale of the Ox herder. \n\nBuy Tickets For 5/19 \n\n 
URL:https://osmosis.com/event/spring-garden-tours-osmosis-landscape-and-me
 ditation-garden-2/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:INTO THE LIGHT: Light-filled aintings by Katy Boggs
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260519T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260519T170000
UID:260501d0T0g_3QwU6GI5JBKgPx3g
DESCRIPTION:Katy's paintings are an exploration of light—how it shapes f
 orm\, reveals color\, and defines what we see.\n\n"I am drawn to moments w
 here light is felt as much as seen: filtering through dense leaves\, tower
 ing in the crowns of trees\, glinting off cresting waves\, or softening in
 to the quiet glow of a sunset. Light is everywhere\; without it\, there is
  no seeing. Beyond its physical presence\, it also carries a deeper resona
 nce as a symbol of hope. In a time of uncertainty\, this work seeks to bri
 ng light into the image\, both visually and metaphorically."\n\nReception:
  April 25\, 4 to 6 pm.
LOCATION:Sebastopol Gallery
URL:http://sebastopolgallery.com
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Modern Monks\, Timeless Wisdom
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260519T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260519T203000
UID:260430hTU9lbQ0nEqhMfCRIdZ-jQ
DESCRIPTION:with Kovilo Bhikkhu and Ajahn Nisabho\n\nJoin us for this even
 ing of meditation\, talk\, and discussion with two engaging young monks fr
 om Seattle\, Ajahn Kovilo and Ajahn Nisabho. Both have been ordained for m
 any years in the Thai Forest lineage of Ajahn Chah and have trained in mon
 asteries in Thailand and the US. They are unique as monks in hosting a wee
 kly podcast on their YouTube channel (https://www.youtube.com/@ClearMounta
 inMonastery/podcasts) with noted Buddhist teachers\, including Jack Kornfi
 eld and Joseph Goldstein. They have a large lay community in Seattle suppo
 rting their plans for a new forest monastery within driving distance of th
 e city.\n\nIn this evening program you will hear more about these monks’
  backgrounds and receive fresh teachings in the classical style of Ajahn C
 hah. While the monks are well known to Insight practitioners in the Seattl
 e area\, this will be their first visit to Spirit Rock—but not their las
 t.
LOCATION:Spirit Rock Meditation Center
