BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:AUDITIONS! For THE CEMETERY CLUB at Bay Area Stage Theatre on Broa
 dway!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260519T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260519T210000
UID:260514Ccvq-Z9vxEq4MiCc1Heh6g
DESCRIPTION:Auditions for The Cemetery Club\, A Comedy by Ivan Menchell Di
 rected by Stacey Loew Auditions are May 19\, 20 & 21 at 7:00pm.  Callbacks
  are TBD at the BAS Theatre \\(515 Broadway Street\, Vallejo.\\) Non-AEA s
 mall stipend available.  CAST: 4 women\, 1 man. All roles are open. All ch
 aracters are in their late fifties to early sixties.  I am looking for hig
 h energy actors with great comedic timing. PREPARATION: • Cold read from
  the script. • Come prepared with a New Yorker accent. ALSO LOOKING FOR:
  Stage manager\, tech crew\, stagehands and creative types to make headsto
 nes. Email Stacey at producer@bayareastage.org for more info or with any q
 uestions. REHEARSALS: Mondays through Thursdays 6/1 – 7/30\, 6:30-9:00 \
 \(early rehearsals\\) 6:30 to 10pm \\(closer to opening.\\)  Rehearsal cal
 endar will be made according to size of role and actor's schedule. PERFORM
 ANCES: July 31– August 16 Fri. and Sat. evenings at 8pm\, Sun. Matinees 
 at 3pm.  Cast call is one hour before showtime. ABOUT THE PLAY: This is th
 e story of three ladies\, Doris\, Lucille\, and Ida - great friends who li
 ve in the same Jewish community in Queens. They are all late to middle-age
 d and have become widows within the past few years. The ladies gather regu
 larly to visit their husbands' graves at Forest Hills to stay connected.  
 CHARACTER DESCRIPTIONS: All the characters listed below are presented as o
 lder widows / widower\, between the ages of 55-70. Some physical comedy is
  required. Doris remains fiercely devoted to her late husband and takes he
 r responsibilities as a widow seriously. She is appalled when she discover
 s that Ida is dating again and loudly protests that she's being disrespect
 ful to her late husband.  Doris has heart issues and is not very adventuro
 us. This role requires a bit of cha-cha dancing\, and has wine thrown in h
 er face. Lucille is eager to start dating again\, partly as revenge agains
 t her late husband\, Harry\, who often cheated on her\, but also because s
 he's very lonely.  She is quite the flirt and is very concerned about her 
 appearance. She is jealous of Ida\, who has snagged a good man before she 
 does. This role requires a bit of cha-cha dancing and smoking\, \\(fake ci
 garettes\\) and has milk thrown in her face. Ida is also not used to being
  alone after 39 years of marriage to Murray\, but she doesn't feel ready t
 o start dating again\, at least not until she meets Sam\, the local butche
 r.  They run into each other on one of their visits to the cemetery and sp
 arks fly.   Sam \\(Male\\) has known Ida and Doris long because they have 
 been his long-time customers. He has also recently lost his spouse and aft
 er meeting Ida at the cemetery\, he gradually but firmly eases his way int
 o her life.  Mildred is a minor role with a brief onstage appearance. She 
 plays the “plus one” date of Sam's at a friend’s wedding. A good-loo
 king woman who is able to cause a bit of jealousy from Ida and Lucille.
LOCATION:Bay Area Stage Theatre on Broadway
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/1487395402607289/?acontext=%7B%22event
 _action_history%22%3A[%7B%22mechanism%22%3A%22lov_feed%22%2C%22surface%22%
 3A%22bookmark%22%7D]%2C%22ref_notif_type%22%3Anull%7D
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
