BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:S.R. Laws Acoustic at Cafe Little Deer
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260520T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260520T123000
UID:260514iKjhqNn2QUOIm4GoVXfqLA
DESCRIPTION:S.R. LAWS IS OUT THERE: He approaches songwriting with a passi
 on for songs that we all grew up on. His sound rings a familiar bell in yo
 ur head while still delivering ideas completely unique.  He draws inspirat
 ion from outstanding storytellers like John Hiatt\, Lucinda Williams\, Ste
 ve Earle\, Neil Finn\, Patty Griffin\, R E.M. and Ron Sexsmith\, among oth
 ers. Their music has played a significant role in shaping his artistic jou
 rney. Growing up out there in Northern California\, he developed a unique 
 connection to music early on. His father worked as a trash collector\, and
  he would spend hours sifting through bags of discarded 45 records. Each f
 ind felt like stumbling upon hidden treasures. Some records were covered i
 n dirt and grime\, while others were pristine. The thrill of discovering n
 ew sounds was exhilarating\, and he could hardly wait to drop the needle a
 nd immerse himself in the music. He embarked on a pilgrimage to Texas with
  just two suitcases and $500 in his bank account. His goal was to dive int
 o the vibrant music scene and learn from fellow songwriters. Austin\, know
 n as the "Live Music Capital of the World\," offered countless opportuniti
 es for him to grow as an artist. Open mics and songwriters' nights became 
 his training ground\, where he soaked up every moment\, listening to other
 s share their stories through music. These days\, he resides in Sonoma Cou
 nty\, California\, working hard as a touring artist and singer-songwriter 
 for his original rock band\, The Heartsleeves. He invites everyone to join
  him on this musical journey\, sharing his songs one person at a time in t
 his vast and unpredictable world we live in.
LOCATION:Café Frida Gallery
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/1346565077288850/?acontext=%7B%22event
 _action_history%22%3A[%7B%22mechanism%22%3A%22lov_feed%22%2C%22surface%22%
 3A%22bookmark%22%7D]%2C%22ref_notif_type%22%3Anull%7D
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
