BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Solano Bayshore Resiliency Project - Countywide Online Community M
 eeting #2
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260520T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260520T180000
UID:260508ocI00700GkG9DydZCyjHRw
DESCRIPTION:Join us for our second countywide online community meeting and
  help shape the future of the Solano Bayshore Resiliency Project—a regio
 nal effort to protect people\, neighborhoods\, infrastructure\, and natura
 l areas from sea level rise.\n\nThis one-hour virtual meeting is an opport
 unity for residents of Suisun City\, Fairfield\, Vallejo\, Benicia\, and u
 nincorporated Solano County to learn about the project\, ask questions\, a
 nd share what matters most to you.\n\nWhy Attend?\n\nLearn how sea level r
 ise may affect your community\n\nHear updates on the regional vulnerabilit
 y assessment and action planning\n\nHelp identify local priorities for sho
 reline resilience\n\nParticipate from home -- no travel required\n\nWho Wi
 ll Be There?\n\nCity and county staff from across the Solano Bayshore regi
 on\, along with project partners\, will be available to answer questions a
 nd hear community input.\n\nYour voice is essential to creating a shorelin
 e that is safe\, equitable\, and resilient for generations to come.
LOCATION:Online - Microsoft Teams
URL:https://events.teams.microsoft.com/event/4142ba61-3d5f-47b2-9d09-9eb6a
 f3d08ea@2bdbbc35-0608-44cd-ad9a-e2e74675e07f
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Pond Farm Artist in Residence 2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260520T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260520T000000
UID:260424bghSRQCl4EK7khJSkBC8Jw
DESCRIPTION:Pond Farm Pottery is the former home and studio of renowned ma
 ster potter\, artist\, and educator\, Marguerite Wildenhain\, and a new Na
 tional Historic Landmark. Pond Farm is located above Armstrong Redwoods\, 
 in beautiful Guerneville\, California. Spend your time in a private cabin 
 at Pond Farm Pottery. Breathtaking inspirational views. Miles and miles of
  hiking. 5 minute drive to Armstrong Redwoods\; 15 minute drive to downtow
 n Guerneville for shopping/art/restaurants/wine tasting\; 30 minutes to th
 e Sonoma Coast\; and approximately 1 hr 45 minutes to San Francisco. Pond 
 Farm Pottery offers an Artist-in-Residence \\(AiR\\) program funded by  Ar
 ts in California Parks \, a program of CA State Parks\, Parks California\,
  and California Arts Council.  Click here for more information about AiR a
 t Pond Farm . Visit Pond Farm by registering for a docent-led tour on our 
  events page  Fill out the application here
URL:https://creativesonoma.org/event/pond-farm-artist-in-residence-2026/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
