SUMMARY:Soda Club Firing
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260523T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260523T170000
UID:260508qDgm7HXFn02D4jUcGUh9Gw
DESCRIPTION:Schedule\n\nSaturday\, May 23 from 10:00 AM – 5:00 PM Sunday
 \, May 24 from 10:00 Am – 6:00 PM Tuesday\, May 26 from 4:00 PM – 7:00
  PM\n\nLocation\n\nKiln Shed\n\nExperience Level\n\nIntermediate and Advan
 ced\n\nEvent Categories: Ceramics\, Workshops\n\nAge\\(s\\)\n\n18 and olde
 r\n\nRegistration\n\nRegistration Cost:\n\n$100\n\nMaterials Fee:\n\nInclu
 ded\n\nTotal Registration Cost:\n\n$100\n\nJoin the Julia Soda Firing Club
  for regular cone 6 soda firings—no formal instruction\, just shared kil
 n access and 1 cubic foot of firing space.\n\nAbout the Class\n\nPrerequis
 ites to enroll in Soda Firing Club\n\nMust have taken at least one\, Intro
  to Mid-Range Soda Firing Workshop\n\nBe well versed in protocols for load
 ing the soda kiln\, kiln safety\, equipment and operating safety\, and be 
 willing and able to be unsupervised with the kiln during loading\, unloadi
 ng\, and post firing cleaning of the kiln.\n\nMust have pre-approval from 
 the Director of Ceramics\n\nThe “Julia” Soda Firing Club is designed f
 or folks looking for longterm use with our Soda Kiln\, Julia. The club is 
 led by Studio Monitors\, and a Studio Technician but involves no formal in
 struction in soda firing processes. Without a formalized instructor\, our 
 Soda Club offers a more financially accessible way of having work soda-fir
 ed\, without the need to retake our Intro to Soda Firing workshop courses.
  The Soda Club will run firings monthly or as often as desired and needed 
 depending on participant interest. Unlike our Soda Firing Workshops\, club
  firings will include no instruction on wadding\, slips\, glazes\, or any 
 lectures on the subject of soda firing. As such\, participants must feel c
 omfortable with the safety and care of the equipment\, as well as loading\
 , firing\, and maintenance procedures surrounding the firing process. Each
  participant gets 1 cubic foot of firing space. Tip: Make sure all your po
 ts fit approximately into a milk crate which is 1 cubic foot of space. Thi
 s firing will be chosen by the group to be either oxidation or reduction\,
  and fired to cone 6 with sprayed soda at the end.\n\nMembership has its b
 enefits\n\nAll Silver Memberships and above receive 10% off the registrati
 on cost for any class purchase over $40. Materials fees are not discounted
 .\n\nBecome a member today and find community\, connection\, and creativit
 y.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/soda-club-firing/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Angels in America\, Part One: Millennium Approaches
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260523T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260523T223000
UID:260508flXhmrXdoUGifCqf3YUrKA
DESCRIPTION:**By Tony Kushner**\n\n**Directed by Steven David Martin**\n\n
 Set in 1980s New York City\, a gay man is abandoned by his lover when he c
 ontracts the AIDS virus\, while closeted Mormon lawyer’s marriage to his
  pill-popping wife stalls. And that’s just the tip of the iceberg. Widel
 y described as one of the greatest plays of the 20th century\, *Angels i
 n America* is a complex\, dynamic\, sometimes surrealistic examination of
  the AIDS crisis and homosexuality in the United States\, while touching o
 n universal issues including change\, loss\, identity\, and the challenges
  of finding community in an increasingly fractured society.\n\n**Content W
 arning**: Please be advised that this production contains simulated sex\, 
 graphic depictions of illness\, staged violence\, and is intended for matu
 re (17+) audiences only.\n\nApprox. 3 hours with 2 intermissions.\n\n**May
  8th\, 9th\, 10th\, \\*14th\, 15th\, 16th\, 17th\, 22nd\, 23rd\, 24th.**\n
 \n**Friday and Saturday Shows:** 7:30 PM\n\n**Sunday Matinee:** 2:00 PM\
 n\n**\\*Value Thursday:** 7:30 PM (Pay What You Can)\n\nDoors open 30 min
 utes before showtime.
LOCATION:The Raven Performing Arts Theater
URL:https://raventheater.org/events/angels-in-america-part-one-millennium-
 approaches/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
