DESCRIPTION:Join Lynmar Estate for the ultimate luxury wine and food exper
 ience in the magical setting of Quail Hill Vineyard. Enjoy an elevated\, m
 ulti-course lunch seasonally paired with ultra-premium Pinot Noir and Char
 donnay. During your meal\, Estate Chef David Frakes will make a special ta
 bleside visit to complete your experience.\n\nReservations are required. M
 aximum group size is six guests. View a sample menu here:\n\nhttps://lynma
 restate.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/Collectors-Lunch-Oct-2025.pdf
LOCATION:Lynmar Estate 
URL:https://lynmarestate.com/reservation/type/collectors-lunch-pairing/ 
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Healdsburg Farmers Market: Saturday
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260523T083000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260523T120000
UID:2603126oC4hl-8tUihyaTl_nbdUg
DESCRIPTION:The Healdsburg Certified Farmers Markets began in 1978\, and i
 s one of the original 22 markets to open in the state that year. Featuring
  an abundance of produce and flowers grown in the region\, as well as inno
 vative food products\, delicious foods to eat on site\, and a variety of c
 reative crafts\, this farmers market shines as an example of the diverse a
 nd delicious offerings of this area.
LOCATION:Foley Family Community Pavilion
URL:https://www.healdsburgfarmersmarket.org/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Overeaters Anonymous (OA) Newcomer Meeting
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260523T094500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260523T101500
UID:2602125Mq7FMLCaEm1ZoYDDKy7NQ
DESCRIPTION:**Is Food a Problem for You? You Are Not Alone.**\n\nOvereater
 s Anonymous (OA) is a fellowship of people who support each other in recov
 ering from compulsive eating and food behaviors. If you feel you have a pr
 oblem with food\, OA welcomes you—no matter what your background\, belie
 fs\, or eating habits. \n\nWe hold an in-person newcomer meeting on first
 \, second and fourth **Saturdays of the month from 9:45 - 10:15 AM at** 
 ​**Unitarian Universalist Congregation of Marin\, 240 Channing Way\, San
  Rafael CA 94903**. Contact: Sue M. 415-298-6792​. You may view all Nor
 th Bay OA in-person and online meetings at https://www.northbayoa.org/meet
 ings.html\n\nIn OA\, members experience **spiritual\, emotional\, and phys
 ical recovery** by practicing the **Twelve Steps** and living by their spi
 ritual principles—one day at a time.\n\nOA is **not** a diet club or cal
 orie-counting program.\n\nMembers have different plans of eating.\n\nOA do
 es **not** endorse any specific food plan. \n\nIf food is causing problem
 s in your life\, you don’t have to struggle alone. Recovery is possible\
 , and help is available.\n\n**Visit:** https://www.northbayoa.org/\n\n**Fi
 nd a meeting:** https://www.northbayoa.org/meetings.html
LOCATION:Unitarian Universalist Congregation of Marin
URL:https://www.northbayoa.org/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Saturday Live Music at Spicy Vines feat. Stella Heath
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260523T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260523T180000
UID:260206herCQ0RXUEqXJPLMi_jc7g
DESCRIPTION:Where unforgettable wines\, live music\, and good vibes come t
 ogether.\n\nJoin us every Saturday from 3–6 PM at Spicy Vines for a tast
 ing room experience like no other — where top local musicians from acros
 s the Bay Area meet our award-winning small-lot wines. From Rock & Roll an
 d Blues to Jazz\, Bluegrass\, and Americana\, each weekend brings new soun
 ds and new reasons to raise a glass. \n\nStella Heath Stella Heath\, deli
 vers a wild\, high-spirited fusion of French Gypsy Jazz\, New Orleans swin
 g\, global folk\, and traditionals. \n\nDetails\n\nNo cover. Walk-ins are
  welcome\, but this event tends to fill up quickly\, so we recommend makin
 g a reservation. We are dog and family friendly!
LOCATION:Spicy Vines Winery
URL:https://spicyvines.com/event/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
