BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Flora & Fauna - 6 Week Watercolor Course
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260524T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260524T160000
UID:260225bKOewOZ-m0-xeU5VqSxIjw
DESCRIPTION:In this 6 week course\, participants will learn a unique appro
 ach to watercolor\, intended to alleviate the frustration that many experi
 ence when learning this beautiful yet challenging medium. The class will f
 ocus on strengthening one’s observational skills\, giving the artist a f
 oundation off of which to build their paintings in a step by step layering
  process\, that trains the artist to see value and color\n\nOur subjects w
 ill be flora and fauna - a sampling of plants and animals - fruits\, flora
 ls\, foliage\, and four legged friends. These subjects are great for begin
 ners and experienced watercolor painters alike\; their organic shapes make
  them forgiving drawing subjects\, but their beauty can be a muse for life
 . \n\nThis class will work from life and from photos\, practicing basic d
 rawing skills in addition to watercolor technique. With six class sessions
 \, participants will have the opportunity to develop their skills and buil
 d muscle memory with a medium that often feels like it has a mind of its o
 wn.\n\nAll materials provided.\n\nLocation: 755 Petaluma Ave\, Sebastopol\
 , CA\n\nDates: 6 Sundays - May 17\, 24\, 31\, June 7\, 14\, 21\n\nTime: 1 
 - 4 pm\n\nRegistration Fee: $300\n\nAges: Adults\n\nSkill Level: All Level
 s
LOCATION:Art & Soul Sebastopol
URL:https://www.hannahdrawstrees.com/flora-and-fauna-register-may
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Lifespan of a Fact
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260524T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260524T152500
UID:250804QGp-WPfc6UOYVPVCb5OqfQ
DESCRIPTION:**Truth or Spin? The Fight over Facts.**\n\n***“Designed for
  laughs\, but the play has a provocative undercurrent regarding issues tha
 t make it a compelling piece of theatre.”* —Cincinnati CityBeat**\n\n*
 **The Lifespan of a Fact* is a critically acclaimed Broadway play that del
 ves into the contentious realm where truth and storytelling intersect. The
  narrative centers on Emily Penrose\, the exacting editor-in-chief of a pr
 estigious magazine\, who assigns Jim Fingal\, an ambitious young fact-chec
 ker\, to verify a groundbreaking essay by renowned author John D’Agata. 
 As Jim meticulously scrutinizes the piece\, he discovers numerous embellis
 hments\, igniting a fierce debate over the boundaries of factual accuracy 
 versus creative license. This fast-paced\, blistering comedy offers a time
 ly exploration of the high-stakes world of publishing\, where the quest fo
 r truth becomes a battleground of wit\, ethics\, and editorial judgment.**
 \n\n**The play has been lauded for its sharp dialogue and thought-provokin
 g themes\, prompting audiences to question: In storytelling\, how far can 
 one go before the facts become fiction?**\n\nThursdays\, Fridays & Saturda
 ys @ 7:30pm\, Saturdays and Sundays at 2:00pm Run Time: 85 mins\, no inter
 mission\n\nThursdays Adult $33 Fri/Sat Eve Adult $39.95\; Senior $36.95\; 
 Under 18 $26.95 Sat/Sun Matinee Adult $47.95\; Senior $44.95 \\*All prices
  include fees (707) 523-4185\n\n**boxoffice@6thstreetplayhouse.com**
LOCATION:6th Street Playhouse
URL:https://6thstreetplayhouse.com/shows/2025-26/lifespan-of-a-fact/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
