BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Overeaters Anonymous (OA) Newcomer Meeting in Santa Rosa
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260524T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260524T170000
UID:260212lX4CZhOAsEOggbBW24PiRA
DESCRIPTION:**Is Food a Problem for You? You Are Not Alone.**\n\nOvereater
 s Anonymous (OA) is a fellowship of people who support each other in recov
 ering from compulsive eating and food behaviors. If you feel you have a pr
 oblem with food\, OA welcomes you—no matter what your background\, belie
 fs\, or eating habits.\n\nWe hold an in-person newcomer meeting on **Sunda
 ys from 4:00 – 5:00 PM** **at Christ Church United Methodist\, 1717 Yulu
 pa Ave.\, Room #4\, Santa Rosa**. Contact: Abigail (707) 293-5888. You may
  view all North Bay OA in-person and online meetings at https://www.northb
 ayoa.org/meetings.html .\n\nIn OA\, members experience **spiritual\, emoti
 onal\, and physical recovery** by practicing the **Twelve Steps** and livi
 ng by their spiritual principles—one day at a time.\n\nOA is **not** a d
 iet club or calorie-counting program.\n\nMembers have different plans of e
 ating.\n\nOA does **not** endorse any specific food plan.\n\nIf food is ca
 using problems in your life\, you don’t have to struggle alone. Recovery
  is possible\, and help is available.\n\n**Visit:** https://www.northbayoa
 .org/\n\n**Find a meeting:** https://www.northbayoa.org/meetings.html
LOCATION:Christ Church United Methodist
URL:https://www.northbayoa.org/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Flora & Fauna - 6
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260524T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260524T160000
UID:260515mlLuJrhzxk-6t7PC1wwMFg
DESCRIPTION:In this 6 week course\, participants will learn a unique appro
 ach to watercolor\, intended to alleviate the frustration that many experi
 ence when learning this beautiful yet challenging medium. Instruction will
  focus on strengthening one's observational skills\, which are foundationa
 l to any painting practice. This approach to watercolor teaches the artist
  to see value and color while building your composition in luminous layers
 . Our subjects will be flora and fauna - a sampling of plants and animals 
 - fruits\, florals\, foliage\, and four legged friends. These subjects are
  great for beginners and experienced watercolor painters alike\; their org
 anic shapes make them forgiving drawing subjects\, but their beauty can be
  a muse for life. Over the course of the class we will progress through 3 
 compositions\, graduating from simpler to more complex forms. This class w
 ill work from life and from photos\, practicing basic drawing skills in ad
 dition to watercolor technique. With six class sessions\, participants wil
 l have the opportunity to develop their skills and build muscle memory wit
 h a medium that often feels like it has a mind of its own. All skill level
 s welcome. All materials provided.
LOCATION:D
URL:https://creativesonoma.org/event/flora-fauna-6-week-watercolor-course-
 with-hannah-day/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
