BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:INTO THE LIGHT: Light-filled aintings by Katy Boggs
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260525T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260525T170000
UID:260501FKt9reKBDECJf4T2qWkPqg
DESCRIPTION:Katy's paintings are an exploration of light—how it shapes f
 orm\, reveals color\, and defines what we see.\n\n"I am drawn to moments w
 here light is felt as much as seen: filtering through dense leaves\, tower
 ing in the crowns of trees\, glinting off cresting waves\, or softening in
 to the quiet glow of a sunset. Light is everywhere\; without it\, there is
  no seeing. Beyond its physical presence\, it also carries a deeper resona
 nce as a symbol of hope. In a time of uncertainty\, this work seeks to bri
 ng light into the image\, both visually and metaphorically."\n\nReception:
  April 25\, 4 to 6 pm.
LOCATION:Sebastopol Gallery
URL:http://sebastopolgallery.com
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Memorial Day
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260525T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260525T115000
UID:260425rc0zAj7cAE2Cls2ne-qIxg
DESCRIPTION:Annual Memorial Day Ceremony behind Vallejo City Hall\, Sponso
 red by https://www.cityofvallejo.net/ and https://davwebsites.dav.org/ca/2
 1/SystemPages/Home.aspx\n\nKeynote speaker: Mayumi Kimura - Deputy Secreta
 ry for Women Veterans Affairs at the California Department of Veterans Aff
 airs\, where she leads the state's mission to serve and honor California's
  more than 150\,000 women veterans and their families by connecting them w
 ith earned benefits through education\, advocacy\, and direct services. Un
 der her leadership\, CalVet Women Veterans Affairs contributes to the stat
 e's mission to ensure all California veterans are the most connected\, pro
 tected\, and respected in the nation.\n\nMayumi is a U.S. Navy veteran and
  a licensed clinical social worker with more than a decade of experience w
 orking with veterans in psychiatric care\, crisis response\, correctional 
 mental health\, and hospice care. She later founded a multi-state mental h
 ealth practice focused on serving underserved and underrepresented communi
 ties. She is recognized as a subject matter expert in PTSD\, military sexu
 al trauma\, and suicide postvention for servicemembers\, veterans\, first 
 responders\, and their families.​
LOCATION:Vallejo Warriors' Memorial
URL:https://www.cityofvallejo.net/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
