BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Soda Club Firing
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260526T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260526T190000
UID:2605086okEBGRysUGUyn0lq4nZfw
DESCRIPTION:Schedule\n\nSaturday\, May 23 from 10:00 AM – 5:00 PM Sunday
 \, May 24 from 10:00 Am – 6:00 PM Tuesday\, May 26 from 4:00 PM – 7:00
  PM\n\nLocation\n\nKiln Shed\n\nExperience Level\n\nIntermediate and Advan
 ced\n\nEvent Categories: Ceramics\, Workshops\n\nAge\\(s\\)\n\n18 and olde
 r\n\nRegistration\n\nRegistration Cost:\n\n$100\n\nMaterials Fee:\n\nInclu
 ded\n\nTotal Registration Cost:\n\n$100\n\nJoin the Julia Soda Firing Club
  for regular cone 6 soda firings—no formal instruction\, just shared kil
 n access and 1 cubic foot of firing space.\n\nAbout the Class\n\nPrerequis
 ites to enroll in Soda Firing Club\n\nMust have taken at least one\, Intro
  to Mid-Range Soda Firing Workshop\n\nBe well versed in protocols for load
 ing the soda kiln\, kiln safety\, equipment and operating safety\, and be 
 willing and able to be unsupervised with the kiln during loading\, unloadi
 ng\, and post firing cleaning of the kiln.\n\nMust have pre-approval from 
 the Director of Ceramics\n\nThe “Julia” Soda Firing Club is designed f
 or folks looking for longterm use with our Soda Kiln\, Julia. The club is 
 led by Studio Monitors\, and a Studio Technician but involves no formal in
 struction in soda firing processes. Without a formalized instructor\, our 
 Soda Club offers a more financially accessible way of having work soda-fir
 ed\, without the need to retake our Intro to Soda Firing workshop courses.
  The Soda Club will run firings monthly or as often as desired and needed 
 depending on participant interest. Unlike our Soda Firing Workshops\, club
  firings will include no instruction on wadding\, slips\, glazes\, or any 
 lectures on the subject of soda firing. As such\, participants must feel c
 omfortable with the safety and care of the equipment\, as well as loading\
 , firing\, and maintenance procedures surrounding the firing process. Each
  participant gets 1 cubic foot of firing space. Tip: Make sure all your po
 ts fit approximately into a milk crate which is 1 cubic foot of space. Thi
 s firing will be chosen by the group to be either oxidation or reduction\,
  and fired to cone 6 with sprayed soda at the end.\n\nMembership has its b
 enefits\n\nAll Silver Memberships and above receive 10% off the registrati
 on cost for any class purchase over $40. Materials fees are not discounted
 .\n\nBecome a member today and find community\, connection\, and creativit
 y.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/soda-club-firing/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A Benefit Concert for Ukraine: Kommuna Lux
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260526T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260526T193000
UID:2605082-I_rJXSZUqOniGstub-5A
DESCRIPTION:$25 General Admission\n\nDoors at 7:30pm. \n\nShow from 8:15-1
 0:30pm with one intermission\n\nAll-Ages are welcome\n\nThis event is a fu
 ndraising concert to benefit the people of Ukraine. KMLX\, our 501-c3 nonp
 rofit\, supports the Burn Unit Beds project of the Rotary eClub of Ukraine
 \, and many grassroots assistance projects in and near Odesa.\n\nKommuna L
 ux: Odesa Urban Folk. Come fall in love with Odesa\, Ukraine\, the Pearl 
 of the Black Sea! Kommuna Lux brings you the heritage music of their belov
 ed hometown. Klezmer\, Balkan\, and Urban Chanson\, with a dash of Ukraini
 an Folk and powered by rocket fuel\, Kommuna Lux impacts the crowd with a 
 nostalgic\, high-energy Big Band sound from the bygone days of speakeasies
  and rum runners. When Volodymyr Gitin raises that clarinet to his lips\, 
 he becomes the only man in the room—you can’t help but utterly fall in
 to his virtuoso arms. “Heavyweight Champion” Oleg Vasianovich holds hi
 s accordion like it’s light as a feather\, while he develops the foundat
 ion of each melody. Layers of complexity are added by the bold\, bright tr
 umpet of Sergei Zhuravel and the sassy\, playful trombone of Yaroslav Besh
 . Keep an eye on drummer Sergei Poltorak—you’ll never know when he’l
 l pause on the percussion to punk the rest of the band with a sly prank. A
 t center stage is sultry powerhouse Bagrat Tsurkan\, whose hot buttered vo
 ice and nonstop energy compel everyone to the dance floor. People don’t 
 just listen to Kommuna Lux. They fall in love! No one can resist these pla
 yful\, passionate Ukrainian musicians\, who have so much fun on stage that
  you get caught up in their joy. https://kommunalux.com/ https://www.faceb
 ook.com/KOMMUNA.LUX https://www.instagram.com/kommuna.lux/ https://www.you
 tube.com/@KommunaLux/\n\nRecommended If You Like: The Klezmatics\, Gogol B
 ordello\, Benny Goodman
LOCATION:The Lost Church
URL:https://thelostchurch.my.salesforce-sites.com/ticket#/instances/a0FUh0
 00008PBOgMAO
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Profs & Pints Napa: Creativity\, Moods\, and Mania
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260526T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260526T180000
UID:2605040KlDxHIkaU66Y0fkCWM3tQ
DESCRIPTION:Profs and Pints Napa presents: “Creativity\, Moods\, and M
 ania\,” an exploration of how depression\, mania\, and everyday ups and
  downs influence different types of creativity\, with Sheri L. Johnson\, d
 istinguished professor of psychology and director of a bipolar disorder re
 search program at the University of California at Berkeley. \n\nAncient q
 uotes on creativity\, moods and mood disorders abound. Aristotle wrote\, 
 “No great mind has ever existed without a touch of madness.” Lord Byro
 n\, describing poets\, later observed\, “We of the craft are all crazy. 
 Some are affected by gaiety\, others by melancholy\, but all are more or l
 ess touched.”   \n\nBut is there really a link between moods\, mood d
 isorders\, and creativity? What does modern science have to say about the 
 subject?\n\nExplore such questions with Dr. Sheri L. Johnson\, director of
  the CALM \\(Cal Mania\\) Program at UC-Berkeley. Her research there studi
 es how mood—especially the highs and lows of bipolar disorder—shapes p
 eople’s lives\, including their creativity\, goals\, and well-being\, as
  well as what mechanisms contribute to mood episodes and recovery.\n\nShe'
 ll begin with a discussion of how scientists measure creativity in life an
 d in the laboratory\, describing what we have learned from hundreds of exp
 erimental studies on creativity and mood. Some findings indicate that happ
 iness\, at modest levels\, can help foster creativity\, while negative moo
 ds can interfere with it. We’ll consider how we can draw from these scie
 ntific findings to protect our own creativity. \n\nTurning to mood disord
 ers\, Professor Johnson will describe how mania was a well-documented part
  of the lives of major creative figures such as Lord Byron\, Vincent Van G
 ogh\, Virginia Woolf\, Edgar Allen Poe\, Ernest Hemingway\, and Alfred Ten
 nyson. \n\nBeyond biographical summaries\, she’ll highlight findings of
  a country-wide study of the Swedish population which connected higher cre
 ativity to a personal and family history of bipolar disorder. She’ll als
 o outline findings of studies designed to test why mood disorders might re
 late to creativity\, and we’ll consider the evidence so far on whether m
 edications for bipolar disorder help or hinder creativity among those with
  a history of mania. \\(Tickets available only online. Advance tickets: $1
 3.50 plus processing fees. Doors: $17\, or $15 with a student ID. Doors op
 en at 5:30 and the talk begins at 6:30.\\)\n\nImage: From a self-portrait 
 painted by Vincent van Gogh in 1889 after slicing off his own ear \\(Court
 ald Institute of Art / Wikimedia\\).
LOCATION:Napa Yard
URL:https://events.ticketleap.com/tickets/profsandpints/napa-creativity-mo
 ods-mania
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:INTO THE LIGHT: Light-filled aintings by Katy Boggs
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260526T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260526T170000
UID:260501JO_QZn0UpE-TXrQ36vmbXQ
DESCRIPTION:Katy's paintings are an exploration of light—how it shapes f
 orm\, reveals color\, and defines what we see.\n\n"I am drawn to moments w
 here light is felt as much as seen: filtering through dense leaves\, tower
 ing in the crowns of trees\, glinting off cresting waves\, or softening in
 to the quiet glow of a sunset. Light is everywhere\; without it\, there is
  no seeing. Beyond its physical presence\, it also carries a deeper resona
 nce as a symbol of hope. In a time of uncertainty\, this work seeks to bri
 ng light into the image\, both visually and metaphorically."\n\nReception:
  April 25\, 4 to 6 pm.
LOCATION:Sebastopol Gallery
URL:http://sebastopolgallery.com
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
