BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:GUIDE DOGS FOR THE BLIND'S GRADUATION CEREMONIES MELT HEARTS
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260530T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260530T143000
UID:260314sQUneq2L00yOovUnZyVmsg
DESCRIPTION:Guide Dogs for the Blind \\(GDB\\) will celebrate its guide d
 og team graduates every other Saturday with public graduation ceremonies a
 t the organization’s campus in San Rafael. These touching public events 
 have inspired tears in even the most stoic audience members\, as graduatin
 g guide dog teams proudly take the stage. Families are welcome at the cere
 monies\, which honor the independence and companionship that GDB’s gui
 de dogs provide for GDB’s clients who are blind or visually impaired. T
 he events also allow GDB’s clients to meet the puppy raisers who cared 
 for their canine heroes prior to beginning formal training at GDB’s cam
 pus. Ceremonies also recognize recent graduates of GDB’s Orientation an
 d Mobility \\(O&M\\) Program\, K9 Buddy Program\, and Breeder Dog Program
 .\n\nAdmission is free\, and Kleenex will be provided. Pre-registered bus 
 groups are welcome. Public tours of the campus are offered on the days of 
 the ceremonies. Visit www.guidedogs.com for more information. Graduat
 ion events are also livestreamed at https://www.youtube.com/@gdb\\_offici
 al/streams.
LOCATION:Guide Dogs for the Blind
URL:https://www.guidedogs.com/about-guide-dogs-for-the-blind/graduations
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:St. Helena Hospital Foundation: The Best is Yet to Come Gala
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260530T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260530T220000
UID:260312Hduhil2FG0G_48Lp6IgJaA
DESCRIPTION:✨🎟️ TICKETS ARE ON SALE — “THE BEST IS YET TO COME
 ” GALA\n\nSlip into your black tie best and cue the music… the night o
 f the season awaits.\n\nInspired by the timeless style of Sinatra\, the St
 . Helena Hospital Foundation invites you to an unforgettable evening at th
 e legendary Louis M. Martini Winery — all in support of a new community-
 owned Rapid Care & Primary Care Center for St. Helena.\n\n🌙 A Night Des
 igned to Dazzle\n\n✨ A show-stopping plated dinner by Chef Nash ✨ Worl
 d-class live entertainment by Élan Artists ✨ Dancing under the stars 
 ✨ A high-energy auction ✨ Glamorous surprises throughout the evening\n
 \nAll wrapped in timeless Sinatra style and Napa Valley sophistication.\n\
 n💖 Beauty with a Purpose\n\nThis dazzling evening will help bring to li
 fe a new integrated Rapid Care & Primary Care Center\, providing:\n\n• 1
 2 hours a day\, 7 days a week care • Immediate treatment for non-emergen
 cy needs • Long-term primary care for children\, adults\, and seniors\n\
 nA permanent\, community-owned healthcare center designed to serve St. Hel
 ena for generations.\n\n🥂 Your Seat at the Table of Change\n\nCare clos
 e to home happens when a community comes together. Join us for a night of 
 glamour\, generosity\, and impact — and help ensure that for St. Helena\
 , the best truly is yet to come.\n\n✨ Get your tickets ✨ Dress to impr
 ess ✨ Come fly with us toward a healthier tomorrow\n\nAfter all… this 
 is our kind of town.\n\n🎟️ Tickets are on sale now.\n\n📧 Shhfounda
 tion@ah.org 📞 707.963.6208
LOCATION:Louis M Martini Winery
URL:https://shhfoundation.org/special-events/gala2026/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
