BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Short Story: Sugarloaf History Hike
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260606T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260606T110000
UID:260504CNYIqNpDIkqCm9YEuA1ILA
DESCRIPTION:This generally gentle (but with a hill climb of a co
 uple hundred feet) hike will loop around the lower areas of the
  park and discuss the park history\, from Native Americans to h
 omesteaders all the way up to the current day. This is the sin
 gle best hike to get an overview of the human history of this
  landscape.\n\nMeet at the White Barn parking lot. Tickets are $
 10 for general admission\, $5 for students\, youth (12-17 year o
 lds)\, Sugarloaf members\, Sugarloaf or RFO volunteers\, and free
  for children under 12. All children under 18 must be accompani
 ed by a parent or legal guardian. **Tickets day-of on site are
  $15 and might not be available**.\n\nWear appropriate clothing a
 nd comfortable shoes\, bring layers\, at least a quart of water\
 , and if desired\, a snack. Parking fees apply.
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/2026junhistory
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Live Music Saturday
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260606T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260606T200000
UID:260502c_C0yalSy0WIsMqy7CIwIA
DESCRIPTION:Tori Roze & Johnny Alexander This is Soul for today: tight\, s
 ophisticated\, and up-to-date...a winner" \\(San Diego Troubadour\\). Tori
  Roze and Johnny Alexander are two members of a larger six piece original 
 funky soul-jazz band called Tori Roze and The Hot Mess from San Diego\, CA
 . The band\, of which Alexander and Roze are the primary songwriters\, has
  been nominated for seven San Diego Music Awards including "Best Acoustic 
 Performer\," "Best Blues Album\," and "Best Pop Album." Tori funnels her m
 usical influence down from childhood favorites Michael Jackson\, Erykah Ba
 du\, Ella Fitzgerald\, Bjork\, Whitney Houston\, and musical theatre - bri
 nging forth a uniquely syncopated\, clever\, interesting\, and unmatched b
 lending of audio tapestries. Alexander\, a diverse man of music ranging fr
 om The Smiths to jazz and classic rock\, is a sound magician inverting sta
 ndard chord structures and time signatures into beautiful landscapes\; his
  contributions are full of brilliant luminescence. As musical atmospheric 
 chameleons\, their desire is to bring forth a deeply emotionally-connected
  performance to every audience who has the pleasure of seeing them. Tori R
 oze & The Hot Mess · Collabs
LOCATION:Ferry Taproom
URL:https://www.mareislandbrewingco.com/events/live-music-saturday-0606202
 6
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Spirit Guides Guided Walking Tour
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260606T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260606T113000
UID:260427BM6Rl89r8k6ZDpW14aGhDg
DESCRIPTION:Join knowledgeable volunteer Garden Guides for special tours o
 f Spirit Guides at Sonoma Botanical Garden on select Saturdays during the 
 run of the exhibition. Experience the updated entrance to our California O
 aks Trail and discover the vibrant\, monumental sculptures by Jacobo and M
 aría Ángeles\, hearing stories about the works’ cultural inspirations\
 , symbolic meanings\, and connections with the natural world. Our voluntee
 rs will enrich your visit with insights into the artists’ process\, the 
 Zapotec influences behind the spirit animals\, and how the exhibition comp
 lements the surrounding landscape. These engaging English language tours o
 ffer context and conversation that deepen your appreciation of both the ar
 t and the Garden.
LOCATION:Sonoma Botanical Garden
URL:https://sonomabg.org/visit/spirit-guides/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Plein Air Sketching Workshop with Hannah Day
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260606T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260606T133000
UID:2604251eOKLXo5EUumXbyg9ENDvg
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy a morning in the garden while sketching the seasonal flo
 wers\, foliage\, and the sculpture of Spirit Guides: Fantastical Creatures
  from the Workshop of Jacobo and María Ángeles. In this one day workshop
 \, participants will learn and practice foundational drawing techniques wh
 ile sketching both organic and constructed forms\, creating a unique compo
 sition of art and nature. Discover the meditative benefits of a plein air 
 art practice\, and gain a deeper appreciation for the natural world around
  you through close observation and intentional rendering. All materials ar
 e provided and all experience and skill levels are welcome!\n\nAbout the I
 nstructor:\n\nHannah Day is a local artist working primarily in the paper 
 arts. She received her MFA in printmaking from University of Hawaii at Man
 oa before returning to Sonoma County\, where she now teaches watercolor\, 
 drawing\, and paper cutting. Day's etchings have been internationally show
 n and collected\, but her current personal practice is focused in graphite
  and watercolor.
LOCATION:Sonoma Botanical Garden
URL:https://sonomabotanicalgarden.ticketing.veevartapp.com/tickets/view/li
 st/plein-air-sketching-workshop-1030-am-130-pm
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
